== T-17: NOT RUN ON THE OVS PLANE, and this is a decision with a reason, not an omission ==
   N-4 SIGSTOPs a SWITCH PROCESS. On P4 that is one simple_switch_grpc per switch, which is
   what the catalogue's live answer was measured against. On this plane there is exactly ONE
   process serving all ten bridges:
        1279 Wed Sep  2 12:19:50 2026 ovs-vswitchd
   SIGSTOPping it would freeze all 10 switches at once -- not the fault N-4 describes -- and
   ovs-vswitchd is the HOST daemon that was already running before this round started
   (2026-09-02 CHECKPOINT (d): 'it is the host daemon ... Leave it alone').
   T-17 therefore needs the P4 plane. Recorded as BLOCKED-ON-THIS-PLANE, not as a pass.
